WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Watched
the first episode of this.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.302 line:92%
I found it really engaging.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember where you were
when this all happened,

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, of course, when
you watch stories like these,

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you go, "Oh, 1993.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember this being
on the news all the time."

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.678 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I was 12 years old.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
I was also 12.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.582 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:20.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I remember
just that last terrible shot

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the compound in flames,
to be honest.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.424 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I don't even know

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.693 size:81% position:41%
if I really remember
that part at that age.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.195
But, obviously, growing up
or learning some history,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
being from Canada or whatnot.
-Whoo!

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
The one other one.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's my mom,
by the way.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.474 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, so that's really
all I really remember.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.344
-It's interesting 'cause I think
that's true of a lot of us.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.345 line:92%
We remember the tail end of it.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
this story takes you back.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the things,
which, of course, makes sense,

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.984 size:75% position:38%
when he was followed
by so many people,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:54.220 size:81% position:41%
is there is a charisma
and likability to him.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.990 line:92%
So you're not playing a mad man

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much
as you're playing somebody

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.493 size:84% position:42%
who had this ability
to connect with people.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that a strange way
to approach it?

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's
the right way to approach it.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, obviously,
during the siege,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.967 line:92%
it was very sensationalized

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
and one-sided
with the press and whatnot.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Dividians
were cut off from the press.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.542
So I think what we're doing here
is basically humanizing

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.810 line:92%
not only Dave but the Dividians

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
and their families,
the followers.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:23.349
And what he was so good at
was giving them purpose.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think everyone
searches for that

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:29.189
at some time in their life,
multiple times and whatnot.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.423 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And he was a messenger,

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:31.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
self-proclaimed
messenger of God.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:35.595
So if he had no followers,
he's got no purpose, as well.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he needed them
as much as they needed him.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was based
on a couple of books.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-A couple FBI guys

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then a guy
who was in the Dividians.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.538 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah, David Thibodeau.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we optioned
Gary Noesner's book,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.208 line:92%
who was the lead FBI negotiator.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's who
Michael Shannon plays, right?

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mike Shannon, yeah.
Up-and-coming, green actor.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.681
-Yeah, it might work out.
Might work out for him.

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He's amazing.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.884 line:92%
-Yeah, he's a great actor.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.985 line:92%
-Yeah, and then David Thibodeau,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the nine survivors
of the final siege.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was on set every day,
you know?

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.892 line:92%
And I think that's, like,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
the ultimate flattery
and validation, you know?

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:12.665 line:92%
Day one was a sermon about joy

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.368 size:84% position:42%
and being a Dividian,
and that was a big one.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he was there
on day one, obviously,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:21.341
and that was -- to have him
kind of tip the hat was --

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just let me
fly from there on.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.745
-Obviously, you had to do a lot
of Bible study for this role.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.047
You also had to lose a lot
of weight for this role.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:28.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-30.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also had to learn
how to play guitar

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sing a little bit
'cause he was a musician.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:35.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that
the most intimidating part?

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh...

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.424
I think
it's all-encompassing, for sure.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I mean, I was
getting voice lessons in L.A.,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:42.996 line:92%
and it was the second time,

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.698
and I was, like, nowhere
even near of hitting any notes.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.568
-Your second voice lesson?
-Yeah, second voice lesson.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get in there, walk in,
and it was --

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:54.407
You know, there's a gal that
was doing Broadway or whatnot

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
right with the piano
and the teacher.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I literally just sat back,
and she was incredible.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:02.549
And they went like five minutes
over, and they stop,

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm kind of
just sitting there,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
just, you know,
listening, loving it.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.989
And, she's like, "Oh, my God.
I'm so sorry. I'm a big fan.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just ran over,"
and I'm like, "Well..."

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking
to the coach at this point.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"Well, you start at a 10,

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then now we're gonna start
like below zero,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.633
and, like,
I'm gonna make your ears bleed."

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's the depressing
thing when you go

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you realize people
who are great

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.138 line:92%
are also getting voice lessons.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were like,
"Oh, I thought this was all

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.341 line:92%
for people who were terrible."

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:33.146
-There's, like, a picture of
Celine Dion right next to me.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I got a feeling
you and Celine

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
weren't starting
from the same --

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.318
It's not a level playing field.
-No.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to ask,
"Friday Night Lights,"

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
fantastic show.
-Thank you.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.489 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm assuming you get
approached all the time.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do people
approach you in that show?

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:54.133
Like, is there just an emotional
connection constantly?

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One, they want to get drunk
with Tim Riggins.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:57.637 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which, yeah,
Tim would do that a lot.

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.307 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.911
-No, I mean, I live in Austin,
Texas, which is an amazing city,

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so it's --
obviously, being in Texas,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.281 line:92%
you get a bit more of it.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:12.285
But people, you know,
are just incredibly flattering,

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they want to have a drink
with you 90% of the time

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.322 size:75% position:38% line:92%
or talk about Coach.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who still
lives in Austin, as well.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.159 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That, I feel like --

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.527 line:92%
You're making it hard for people

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
by living in the city
it was filmed,

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you can't say to them,
"Hey, that's not me,"

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.000
and they'd be like, "Well,
then you should've moved."

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, totally.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm still
living in the past, I think.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I'm gonna
make a weird leap here,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
but David Koresh
was a failed musician,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
to some degree, or a musician.
-Yes.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there is something
about music and sermonizing

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:41.614 line:92%
and connecting with an audience

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.082 size:81% position:41%
in the same way you do
as a religious leader.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we share a great love
of Bruce Springsteen.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:47.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we do.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.790 line:92%
-And he's on Broadway right now.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.591 line:92%
I thought -- I actually --

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was very close to
a religious experience for me.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You went a couple nights ago?

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-How was it?

00:04:57.664 --> 00:05:00.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man.
He raised me, that guy.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He really did.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just...
I was just blown away.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cried, I laughed.
It's just --

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
As much
as he's telling his story,

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just --
he takes you back.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just like
you remember these beats

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:17.183
of your first kiss to, you know,
traveling in the car, obviously,

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the first time
you went camping,

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
or all of these kind of beats
throughout your life.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.022 line:92%
So it was just incredible.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.257 line:92%
-The other thing about it is,

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.793 size:88% position:44%
not the cheapest tickets
you're ever gonna buy.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-And then, I don't --

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
During the show,
I had this realization of,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I would've paid 10 times --"
-Yeah.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:32.965 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-"This is worth 10 --

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the biggest deal
I've ever gotten."

00:05:34.434 --> 00:05:36.736
-I came out of there,
and I went with my best friend,

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:39.839
and I'm like, "I would've
easily paid way more for that."

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was
a life-altering experience.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:44.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I threw money
onstage at the end.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, really?
I threw panties.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
My panties were up there.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.682
-No.
-Thanks so much for being here.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congrats on the show.
Really a pleasure.

